| Cyanotype | `#2244F0` | Primary blue: pixels, primary buttons, focus |
| Periwinkle | `#7B8AF7` | Secondary pixels, the Seed engine |
| Blueprint navy | `#0B1233` | Dark sections |

**Dark sections:** the background is navy, line art is `#3A4470`, text is `#E9ECF7`, and pixels stay cyanotype and periwinkle. They should read like a blueprint, not black.

**Harvest and Seed:** the old HTML used amber and teal for the two engines. Here they become **solid cyanotype pixels** for Harvest and **outlined periwinkle pixels** for Seed.

### Type

| Face | Role | Settings |
|---|---|---|
| **Newsreader** (Google Fonts, variable, optical sizes) | Headlines, body, buttons | Headlines weight 300–400, tracking −1%, line-height 1.05. Body weight 400, 18–20px, line-height 1.55. |
| **IBM Plex Mono** | Drawing annotations only: callouts, metric values, source names, figure captions | 12–13px, sentence case. Never used for headings or paragraphs. |

The type scale is 88 / 64 / 40 / 24 / 19 / 13 on desktop and 48 / 40 / 28 / 20 / 17 / 12 on mobile.

Claude's own serif is proprietary. Newsreader is the closest free match, with the same light, bookish display feel, and Source Serif 4 is the fallback option.

Two type rules apply everywhere:
- Headlines are one color. There is no highlighted word, because the drawings carry the emphasis.
- There are no all-caps eyebrow labels above headings.

### Texture

- **Dot grid** on light sections: 24px spacing, `#E3E6EE` dots, taken from reference image 2.
- **Square pixel grid** only in dark sections, as the field the pixel art lives on, taken from reference image 1.

### Layout: the drawing sheet

Each section is laid out like one sheet from an architectural drawing set. The drawing gets the big field, and the words sit in a title block anchored bottom-left. Text is always left-aligned, with a 1200px max width on a 12-column grid.

```
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                                                          │
│            DRAWING FIELD (line art + pixels)             │
│                  ── callout ──●                          │
│                                                          │
├───────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────┤
│ Headline              │                                  │
│ One line of body.     │  (optional: CTA or interaction)  │
│ Fig. 4  caption       │                                  │
└───────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────────┘
```

On mobile, the drawing goes on top, the title block sits below it, and callouts collapse into a list under the drawing.

### Components

- **Primary button:** a cyanotype fill with white Newsreader text and a 2px radius.
- **Secondary action:** an ink text link with an underline. No arrows are appended to button text.
- **Callout:** a leader line from a point on the drawing to a mono annotation, styled like a dimension line on a blueprint. This is how investor metrics are woven in (see section 3).
- **Tile:** used for trust and audiences. It has a hairline border, no shadow and square corners.
- **Title block:** headline, one line of body, and a figure caption.

### Motion

The page has one orchestrated moment: the **hero scan**. On load, the line art draws in, then a vertical scan edge sweeps left to right over about 1.6s and leaves blue pixels on three "invention" spots.

Everything else is static unless the user acts: the how-it-works stepper, the evidence graph nodes, the FAQ accordion. With `prefers-reduced-motion`, the page shows the end state immediately.

