## 3. Investor weave: callouts

Investor information lives as **annotations on the drawings**, the way an architect marks dimensions and materials. A user can ignore them, and an investor scanning the page picks up the whole story.

- Each section has at most two callouts.
- A callout has the form `value` + a short label, for example `{{ARR}}  annual recurring revenue`.
- Only **public-safe** metrics go on the page. Sensitive ones, such as margin, burn and NRR, go behind an "Investors" link in the footer. See the registry in section 5.

**The story the callouts tell, top to bottom:**
traction, then market, then speed and quality, then land-and-expand, then moat, then a second market (agencies), then pricing model, then trust.

